{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Afternoon. Grab a seat. What's brought you in?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Back.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): Whereabouts?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Low. Middle.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): How long has it been sore?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Weeks.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): A few weeks, or since the move? I saw a note that you'd shifted house.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): The move. Bakkie full of boxes. Or before. Dunno.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): Shame, that's hectic. You still at the warehouse, doing the physical work?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): Parking was a proper mess this morning, never mind. On a bad day, out of ten?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Seven.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): What sets it off?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Bending.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): Does a rest ease it?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Ja.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any numbness or tingling down the legs? I always ask, because that changes things.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): And the bladder? Any leaking, or trouble getting the water going?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Up at night. Twice. For years.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): So that's old, not from this. No leaking though, and the stream is fine?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): No leaking. Fine.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): Weight coming off at all?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): Belt's looser. Maybe. Not weighed.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): A maybe, then, no number. Any fever, or night sweats?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): Which pain tablets are you on?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): Ibuprofen.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): The nurse wrote four hundred milligrams three times a day in the notes. Is that the dose?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Two hundred.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): Two hundred milligrams. How often do you actually take it?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Twice. Sometimes I skip.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): So the file and what you swallow don't agree, and it's hit and miss. Ever had an x-ray of this back?",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Last year. Borderline, they said.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): Borderline, and no figure attached. Let me press. Muscle here's tender. Midline bone is not.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): Sore.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (DOCTOR): Straight leg raise is clear both sides. No numb patches, no weak feet. I'm calling it mechanical low back pain from the lifting, not a nerve pinch. No scan from me today.",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (DOCTOR): Stay on the move, short walks, a hot bottle if you fancy it. Bring the ibuprofen box next time so we can settle the dose. If it's not better in two weeks, come back. Sooner if a leg goes numb, you can't pass water, or you get a fever."
 ],
